mantle rm297
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_knut_sootley
title the covered ember
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=sailor
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk checks_a_straw_for_smoke_before_saying_where_its_been
likes plum_tart digging fresh_straw warm_rain
dislikes drizzle stale_bread
fears a_tally_rubbed_out a_rope_taking_the_weight_early
hopes dry_straw_to_spare a_patch_of_ground_alone
topics work +0.4 pastimes +0.4 prices +0.3 gossip -0.4 weather +0.3
styles gossip=secretive refuse=sharp comfort=material tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# draws a straw from a smoke-scented cuff, can pick the sound side of a battered crate by touch and takes unkindly to questions about either talent.

words
oath! = Soot in the tally | Splinter my hoop
saying! = A stalk remembers where the weight lay | Count the lift twice
straw = my clean straw | a fresh yellow stalk
stain = a black dust mark | the smoke smudge
wedge = a loose packing wedge | the flat wood chip
crate = the bare end board | a weathered crate end
past = a rubbed chalk stroke | the ghost of a tally
clod = a square clod | the heavy dirt lump
prong = a broken digging tine | my scrap of fork
rainbit = warm runoff | rain that's lost its chill
pastry = a plum-dark crust | the blistered pastry corner
bread = a sour dry heel | that brick of old bread
fold = my inner cuff | the sleeve's turned edge
stand = a scrap of firm ground | a square of dry boards

any
opinion @1 houses against 3 : Some debts weigh rather more than cargo. No House at the water's edge has a book large enough to enter mine.
opinion @2 merchants against 2 : No beauty to a dear loaf when the teeth go clean through air just under the crust.
opinion @3 dole for 1 : A free bowl can give a wolf some weight to put behind the next lift. That's good enough reason.
opinion @4 sump for 1 : Sump folk don't object if you keep your own account of who gets the lighter end to carry.
opinion @5 watch against 1 : I know a hard question from a heavy boot. Neither makes a light job easier.
opinion @6 times against 2 : They say the load's the same. I've felt what went missing from my end of the bargain.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Stand in the clear if you've a word. | New face. No need to come closer yet.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : So the light got through. Welcome. | Early for asking about anything heavy.
line @3 greet [here.weather=rain] : Wet out. Wipe before you lean. | Rain's come in along with you.
line @4 greet.return : I heard. Here's your greeting back. | Civil words travel cheaply enough.
line @5 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : There's a welcome by the board I'm minding. | A known voice. That's less work.
line @6 farewell : Don't walk under what hasn't settled. | Keep the last dry stalk for yourself.
line @7 farewell.return : I won't hold you at this corner. | Your side's clear to leave by.
line @8 again.open : Back along the same set of tracks. | That's your mark past here twice.
line @9 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come where the kin can hear one another. | My end has room for the family weight.
line @10 hail [pair.band=friends] : Here, off the chalk line! | Down by the clear corner!
line @11 react.news : I'll want the actual weight of that account. | Don't tell me what's written over the original mark.
line @12 react.news.known : I've seen the underside of that particular piece. | That account's got a notch in my memory.
line @13 react.news.new : Fresh stroke on a board I knew bare. | I'd no previous mark for that one.
line @14 react.news.doubt : Show me the stroke somebody rubbed away first. | That tale has gained some weight between the first lift and this one.
line @15 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : There's a place gone empty that somebody still counts. | Leave quiet round it. I know the cost.
line @16 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth] : That's a mark worth leaving up on the board. | Glad there's more than bad debts to reckon.
line @17 answer.how : Doing my own checking. Sufficient. | Still on the end I chose.
line @18 decline : I'll need a clearer account before I put my back behind that. | My time's too dear for a promise that doesn't stand level.
line @19 accept_decline : That's the answer as given, then. | Good. No loose end I have to mind.
line @20 sympathise : I can put a bit of weight on my side for you. | Sit off the corner where the load can't reach.
line @21 thank : A decent turn under a bad weight. | Mark yourself a little extra in your favour.
line @22 deflect_thanks : I didn't fancy being under the loose end either. | You're free to repay it somewhere else.
line @23 preclose : Time I checked what I'm standing on. | Some hours stay clear of my ledger.
line @24 accept_preclose : Leave your chalk where it is. | You're done here. Go easy.
line @25 farewell [here.time=night] : Don't trust a painted edge in poor light. | Keep clear of a dark overhang.

scene cuff
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #straw# comes out of #fold# with a smell of wood smoke. | I test a bit of packing by bending it under my nose.
b : Can you say where you've been from that? | What should decent straw smell of?
a : I might. Doesn't follow that I care to say. | Dry sun. If I smell smoke twice I check whether it's my own sleeve.

scene plumcorner
when topic=food self.likes=plum_tart
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I lift #pastry# to see if there's fruit clear underneath. | A tart with a wet bottom tells you how it was packed.
b : You're not paying by the plum, are you? | Wouldn't it just say the plum was juicy?
a : I'm paying for something. I like to meet it while I'm eating. | Then there's good fruit to show for it. My nose tells the rest.

scene strawtest
when topic=pastimes self.likes=fresh_straw
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fresh straw springs twice when you squeeze a fistful. | A flattened stalk keeps its complaint to itself.
b : Twice, specially for your private benefit? | I can hear it crack from here.
a : Once out of my hand. Again when the next weight lands. | That's a sound answer. Straws make poor liars.

scene dig
when topic=pastimes self.likes=digging
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I turn #clod# I study the surface that used to face downward. | One crumble of dirt shows what pressure the last boot left.
b : After coins in the furrow? | More interest in boots than roots?
a : No. I like knowing one square of the world all the way through. | A boot pressed hard leaves air out of a place roots need it.

scene drizzle
when topic=weather self.dislikes=drizzle
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Drizzle puts #stain# halfway up my wrist before I feel wet. | There's a rain so mean you don't hear it working.
b : Can't be much trouble if you don't feel it. | Then why give it a full hearing now?
a : It's already under my sleeve by the time I find the trouble. | Because the straw's soaked. I heard what it failed to warn me about.

scene warmrain
when topic=weather self.likes=warm_rain
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #rainbit# running down my neck is more tolerable than a cold mist. | Warm rain releases the clean dirt smell round a struck spade.
b : You'd still want a decent collar. | What's the value of smelling a furrow?
a : I'll take the warmth without owing the collar an explanation. | Mine to reckon. Nobody's charging admission to it yet.

scene stalebread
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A seller asks fresh coin for #bread#. I object to the difference in age. | Wouldn't trust a shop that hid a stale heel under a bright crust.
b : Coin doesn't go stale like a loaf. | You could soak it without much trouble.
a : And bread doesn't earn interest. Another argument against that price. | I'd like an honest price before I'm volunteered for the extra work.

scene badlift
when topic=work self.job=sailor self.working=yes self.trade_words
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #self.trade_words#. Look at #crate# before you trust the chalk. | I listen for loose wood when the load first comes taut. #self.trade_words#.
b : What can the chalk be hiding? | Can you hear trouble with the pier that noisy?
a : Nothing at all. Or a board somebody's in a hurry to have carried off. | Right through the wrist. Hearing comes in more than one sort.

scene lostpost
when topic=work self.job=sailor
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I have held a better place than the one my elbows know now. | I know how fast a name rubs off a tally when a better-connected one turns up.
b : Ever put in for the old place again? | Did the work itself go anywhere?
a : No. I want a load with room for me to look at either end. | Didn't lose an ounce. Only the old paws got put aside.

scene dockdebt
when topic=times here.region=ridgemere
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : Wharf houses can count every crate except what a load costs a household. | I take little comfort in a handsome port tally.
b : A ledger needn't answer for every trouble. | Would a rough tally suit you better?
a : True. Don't ask me to admire it like it made good all those debts. | One that marked the empty place at supper would be worth reading.

scene sump
when topic=land self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Sump rooms hold smoke after the fire's been cold a week. | Down home I hang a dry stalk high past the flood stain.
b : Can you get the smell out with straw? | Does that do anything to the water?
a : I'm content if fresh straw has a smell of its own for an hour. | No. Gives me a sound bit to test the rest against.

scene quickcoin
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A poor wolf ought to know which corner of a load is all packing. | I don't want a merchant's word included on the scales.
b : Time spent testing might cost you the bargain. | What weight's the word of a decent seller?
a : Let it cost me. A rotten purchase would cost me dearer. | Light enough to leave aside till I've seen the goods.

scene pal
when topic=friends self.friend
does offer / accept / assess
a : I'd save a dry sheaf for #self.friend#. Take this loose stalk. | I've got enough sound plums to put one by for #self.friend#. Want a small one?
b : I'll twist it round the end of my wrapper. | One mouthful would do me.
a : That's sense. Smoke on wrapping can make a parcel smell better than it is. | Try the sound side. I cut the bruised quarter out to check.

scene mixedtalk
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I keep some facts wrapped like a plum against rough boards. | Sharing a tally with a stranger gives the stranger a lot of spare chalk.
b : What's the bruise you're looking to spare? | Would you rub away a mark of your own?
a : The bit where an idle thumb went through something I meant to keep. | No. But I don't leave it beside somebody else's empty figures.

scene chipprong
when topic=pastimes
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : What would you cut a channel with if #prong# can't take the hard top off? | Where's the better spot to turn a shallow bed after heavy rain?
b : Put the heavy spade in at a slant first. | Where you still see little dry cracks.
a : Aye. It gives the tine something to catch hold of. | Good. A furrow with its own water is work for a ditch, not dinner.

scene wrapway
when topic=travel
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll walk two streets extra if it keeps a roof load out of my sky. | I mean to walk a stretch without looking up for a falling slat.
b : Even when the shortcut's perfectly clear? | Which way does that leave you?
a : It looks clear till it isn't. I set my price on the extra walk. | Far side of the road where the load would have to jump. Good enough.

scene bettergarden
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like #stand# wide enough for a bit of digging and a shut gate. | One day I'll plant three crops without chalking the spare inches for a landlord.
b : Which part matters most? | What grows in those odd inches?
a : The latch. On my side. Ground comes next. | Leave them wild to see what the ground was planning.

scene weightcase
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Seems there's a corner off every meal before I get near a knife. | #past# has almost as much meat on it as my supper.
b : Wouldn't a shared pot make that look better? | That's a hungry sort of joke.
a : Only if a wolf can reach the ladle too. I'd watch that part. | I wasn't offering you a laugh. Something substantial to chew would do.

story straw_mark [topic=work]
  : I packed a small crock in fresh straw and set a heavier jar beside it. Somebody wanted to know which had stood where after I took them both out.
  : I put a thumb into the two hollows. One was shallow and had a crushed margin.
  b : Was that the heavier jar?
  : No, the small crock that somebody had taken up and set down twice. A weight can leave a misleading history.

story clean_cuff [topic=smalltalk]
  : A seller had two parcels of straw. Cheap and dear. I smelt the cheap parcel and it smelt of a smoky room, so I took the clean dear bunch first.
  : Halfway home I put it up to my nose again. Same smell.
  b : Had you picked up the wrong bunch?
  : Right bunch. Wrong sleeve. I still think the seller charged for more sun than that straw had seen.

story ground_price [topic=pastimes]
  : I once tried to buy enough soil for a wooden box. Seller held up a handsome clod and knocked it on the board.
  : Sounded hollow. I broke it down the seam with my thumb.
  b : Anything hidden inside?
  : Only air. I bought the loose dark stuff by the scoop and brought my own box.

rule @sleeve
when concept=bark self.likes=fresh_straw
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That's my smoke, not the bundle's. | Dry stalk first. Then the thumb test.

rule @lift
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=sailor
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Turn the chalked board toward my nose. | I can hear that board through my wrist.

rule @mist
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say No honest sound from that mean little wet. | My poor cuff caught the whole soaking.

rule @dug
when concept=bark self.likes=digging
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One more turn to see what's under there. | Ground hasn't made a false entry yet.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : You'll get an answer that fits the business. Tell me what the business is.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. At least we know where the last conversation stood.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Speak in the open. I dislike a question hanging over me in poor light.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Keep your paws well on your side of that mark.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=sailor self.trade_words] : #self.trade_words#. If you need something moved, state the real weight.
dlg @6 resident.job : I like work that shows where the weight changes hands.
dlg @7 resident.bye : Walk wide of the next overhang.

graft resident.hub
choice Can straw really keep an account? -> bent_straw
node bent_straw
say Shows where something heavy lay. Pull the stalk up and the crease points straight at you. Much plainer to my eye than House accounts, and harder to rub out.
choice Can it name the load? -> vague_load
choice Close the account, then. -> hub
node vague_load
say I didn't say it could write a whole description. But I'd take a crease I could feel over a label somebody wants me to trust.
choice I'll look underneath next time. -> hub
choice Enough about the weight. -> bye
